Map the position of a DFT pen to the screen with the pitch and origin of the antenna grid

iptsd takes the first antenna for one edge of the screen and the last one for the other. The
antenna grid of a panel is a little smaller than the screen and need not be centered on it: on
the Surface Pro 9 (273.89 x 182.59 mm, 68 x 46 antennas) the antennas are 4.0748 mm apart in X and
4.0158 mm in Y, and the first one is 0.44 mm (X) and 0.94 mm (Y) from the edge. The pen position
is therefore off by up to 0.44 mm in X and 0.94 mm in Y at the edges, and correct in the middle.

With [DFT] AntennaPitchX / AntennaPitchY (mm per antenna) and AntennaOriginX / AntennaOriginY
(position of antenna 0 in mm from the screen edge) the position is antenna * pitch + origin.
Without them nothing changes. Touch contacts come from the heatmap and are not affected.

Measured by replaying captures of handwriting and comparing with what Windows computes from the
same frames (contact samples of handwriting, before any filtering): median distance 0.27 .. 0.81
mm without the keys, 0.03 .. 0.20 mm with them (the rest is the tilt offset).

